WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:05.800
 From within in our RStudio Cloud workspace, 
  there are four possible roles 

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:10.040
 that an individual can occupy. 
  As the creator of the workspace 

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:13.640
 we are given the default status 
  of administrator, and we cannot change 

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:18.400
 that status. Administrators 
  have full privileges within workspace. 

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:22.320
 Administrators can manage the workspace 
  and all of the projects, 

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:26.160
 including their own, 
  and also view all of the projects 

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:28.840
 within a workspace, 
  including private projects. 

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:32.760
 Moderators have all of the same privileges 
  as an administrator, 

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:37.560
 except that moderators cannot add 
  or remove learners from the workspace. 

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:41.240
 This means that moderators can manage 
  all of the projects, 

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:43.920
 as well as view all of the projects 
  within a workspace. 

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:47.720
 Contributors can create 
  and manage their own projects, 

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:50.880
 and they can also view any projects 
  that have been shared with them. 

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:54.680
 As an administrator or moderator, 
  we can also control 

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:58.480
 whether or not contributors can see the 
  names of other members in the workspace, 

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:02.880
 make their projects visible to all 
  members, and change project resources. 

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.440
 Users have the most 
  restrictive permissions 

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:09.480
 and can only view projects 
  that have been shared with the workspace 

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:13.720
 or with them as an individual. 
  As an administrator or moderator 

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:14.880
 we can also control  

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:18.440
 whether or not a viewer can see the names 
  of other members in the workspace. 

